  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nElections - Benton County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n Benton County\n \nElections\n \n \n\n \n\n Contact Benton County Elections\n \n \n\n \n \nHome\n \nVote\n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections\n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials\n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \nWelcome to the Benton County Elections Website.\n The Election Department in the Auditor’s Office is responsible for every aspect of conducting an election from voter registration to the final count of the votes. This site is designed to be a resource for residents looking to learn how to vote, find their elected officials, learn about becoming a candidate, or find past or upcoming election information.\n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \nQuick Links\n \nRegister to Vote\n \nWhere Do I Vote?\n \nAm I Registered?\n \nHow Do I Vote?\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nElected Officials\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nUpcoming & Recent Elections\n \n\n \n\n \nNov\n \n3\n \n \n\n General 2026 Election\n General Election\n \n\n Election Information Sample Ballot(s)\n Public Notice\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nJun\n \n2\n \n \n\n Primary 2026 Election\n Primary Election\n \n\n Official Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n Candidate List\n Public Notice\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nNov\n \n4\n \n \n\n City/School Election 11-4-2025\n City/School Election\n \n\n Official Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n Candidate List\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n News\n \n\n Courthouse Closure\n \n August 4, 2026 \n\n \n \n\n FY27 Budget Hearing Notice\n \n April 12, 2026 \n \n\n FY27 Proposed Budget\n \n April 12, 2026 \n \nAll News\n \n \n\n \n \n\n Benton County Voter Registration\n \n Updated July 10, 2025\n \n\n\n \n \nLibertarian\n \n\n\n \n106\n \n\n \n \nRepublican\n \n\n\n \n7,250\n \n\n \n \nDemocratic\n \n\n\n \n3,421\n \n\n \n \nNo Party\n \n\n\n \n6,901\n \n\n \n \nOther\n \n\n\n \n22\n \n\n \n \n \n \n Register to Vote\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n Benton County Courthouse\n\n Hayley Rippel, Auditor\n\n Auditor's Office, 2nd Floor\n\n P.O. Box 549\n\n 111 E. 4th Street\n\n Vinton, IA 52349\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n 8:00AM to 4:30PM\n\n Monday - Friday\n \n \nPhone Numbers\n\n Office: (319) 472-2365\n\n Fax: (319) 472-3692\n\n \n \n\n \n\n Contact Benton County Elections\n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
